From a931e92b0f4ca2e6ad99f2930e15f69f1f07c404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Grasso <code@danielgrasso.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:47:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(color): sRGB-tagged SDR decodes like untagged SDR
 under a staged SDR gamut mapping

With untagged SDR decoded by the sdr_transfer curve, a client that tags
its surface as sRGB (Chromium and Electron do) was still decoded with
the piecewise curve: the same color came out as two values, 9 against
14 for code 16 on a gamma 1.8 panel. Under a staged SDR gamut mapping,
sRGB-tagged content in sRGB primaries now takes the pass's SDR curve
too. Content tagged with the output's own description is unchanged.

Harness: color_profile_srgb expects the gamma 2.2 decode, the new
color_profile_srgb_transfer pins sdr_transfer = "srgb", and
color_profile_srgb_tagged pins tagged equal to untagged.
